  "modeling_notes": [
    "The broad 48-credit General concentration is the canonical B.S. path. The 48-credit Cybersecurity and 51-credit Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning paths are preserved as alternate requirement variants rather than being collapsed into one menu.",
    "The canonical unit path keeps the 34 published COLL and Creative/Performing Arts credits distinct from the major. Published overlap is allowed but not required; overlap changes how the 38-credit remaining capacity is used, not the 120-credit degree minimum.",
    "Foreign-language proficiency can be satisfied before matriculation and therefore has a zero-credit canonical increment. Any language coursework still needed is taken inside the remaining degree capacity.",
    "Mathematics proficiency and the major writing requirement are satisfied by named major requirements. COLL 350 is an attribute on another COLL course and carries no additional canonical increment.",
    "Accelerated bachelor's-to-master's pathways, honors, and advising schedules are excluded from the ordinary B.S."
  ],
